course: dictionary
lesson: 6834
title: Outdated words and ideas
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you that something belongs to the past. Look at «"Legacy system" means old, outdated software.» The word legacy shows the software is from earlier times, and outdated tells you it is no longer the newest or best. Context clues like these help you understand the word.
explain: Outdated has two meanings. The first is old-fashioned, or no longer used because something newer exists: outdated phones, clothes or maps. The second is no longer correct because things have changed: outdated information. Try the meaning in the sentence. If "old and replaced" fits, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Outdated ideas in science have often been replaced by better ones. Once people believed Earth was flat, but evidence showed that idea was outdated. When you read about an old idea, check whether the text says it has been replaced.
fact: «Outdated» is an adjective: outdated, more outdated.
fact: «Outdated» means old-fashioned, or no longer correct because things have changed.
fact: «Outdated technology» means machines or devices that newer ones have replaced.
fact: «Outdated information» means facts that are no longer true or correct.
fact: In science, an outdated idea, such as the idea that Earth is flat, has been replaced by a better one.
exercise: «"Legacy system" means old, outdated software.» What does outdated mean here? | Made of wood | *Old-fashioned, and replaced by something newer | Brand new and just released | Very loud and noisy
exercise: Ravi says the book's figures are outdated. What does that suggest? | *The figures are no longer correct, because things have changed | The figures are written in another language | The figures are very funny | The figures are brand new and shiny
exercise: «"Legacy system" means old, outdated software.» Find and copy one word that means no longer the newest. | system | means | software | *outdated
test: Which of these is an example of outdated technology? | A brand-new tablet bought this week | *A floppy disk that newer storage devices have replaced | A sunny day at the beach | A brand-new bicycle
test: In science, which idea is an outdated one? | That Earth goes round the Sun | That plants need light to grow | *That Earth is flat
exam: Which phrase means facts that are no longer correct because things have changed? | *outdated information | outdated technology | bright new software | legacy hardware
